# The build stage compiles the sources itself, so the host's build output and
# Gradle caches must never reach it. BuildKit only sends the paths named by
# the COPY instructions (build scripts, gradle/, app/src/), so today these
# rules do not change the context; they keep the image independent of the
# host if a broader COPY is added, and they apply to builders that send the
# whole context (legacy builder, Buildah/Podman). IDE files and logs likewise.
.gradle/
**/build/
.kotlin/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.log
